DG.put("chandee-charitr-2/6",{"n":6,"title":"ਅਥ ਸੁੰਭ ਜੁਧ ਕਥਨੰ","title_roman":"Ath sunbh judh kathnan","page":228,"blocks":[{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[1,157],"number_text":"੧। ੧੫੭।","page":228,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਘੁੰ ਭ੍ਰਾਤ ਜੁਝਿਯੋ ਸੁਨਿਯੋ ਸੁੰਭ ਰਾਯੰ।","roman":"Laghun bhraat jujhiyo suniyo sunbh raayan |","meaning_en":"King Sumbh heard that his younger brother had fallen in battle;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜਾ ਸੁੰਭ ਨੇ ਜਦੋਂ ਭਰਾ ਦੇ ਮਾਰੇ ਜਾਣ ਦੀ ਖਬਰ ਸੁਣੀ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਜੈ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਅਸਤ੍ਰੰ ਚੜਿਯੋ ਚਉਪ ਚਾਯੰ।","roman":"Sajai sasatr astran chariyo chaup chaayan |","meaning_en":"arming himself with weapons and missiles, he marched out with eager zeal;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਤਦੋਂ) ਉਸ ਨੇ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਅਤੇ ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਜਾਏ ਅਤੇ ਬੜੇ ਚਾਉ ਨਾਲ (ਯੁੱਧ ਲਈ) ਚੜ੍ਹ ਚਲਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਯੋ ਨਾਦ ਉਚੰ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਪੂਰ ਗੈਣੰ।","roman":"Bhayo naad uchan rahiyo poor gainan |","meaning_en":"a loud sound arose and filled the sky;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਹੁਤ ਜ਼ੋਰ ਦਾ ਨਾਦ ਹੋਇਆ (ਜਿਸ ਨਾਲ) ਸਾਰਾ ਅਕਾਸ਼ ਗੂੰਜ ਉਠਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰਸੰ ਦੇਵਤਾ ਦੈਤ ਕੰਪਿਯੋ ਤ੍ਰਿਨੈਣੰ। ੧। ੧੫੭।","roman":"Trasan devtaa dait kanpiyo trinainan | 1 | 157 |","meaning_en":"the gods and demons were afraid, and the three-eyed one (Shiva) trembled. 1. 157.","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ) ਦੈਂਤ ਕੋਲੋਂ ਦੇਵਤੇ ਡਰ ਗਏ ਅਤੇ (ਤ੍ਰਿਨੈਣੰ) ਸ਼ਿਵ ਡਰ ਗਿਆ ॥੧॥੧੫੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2,158],"number_text":"੨। ੧੫੮।","page":228,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਡਰਿਯੋ ਚਾਰ ਬਕਤ੍ਰੰ ਟਰਿਯੋ ਦੇਵ ਰਾਜੰ।","roman":"Dariyo chaar baktran tariyo dev raajan |","meaning_en":"The four-faced one (Brahma) was afraid; the king of the gods moved away;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਟਰਿਯੋ: 'moved aside, withdrew'.","meaning_pa":"ਬ੍ਰਹਮਾ ('ਚਾਰ ਬਕਤ੍ਰੰ') ਡਰ ਗਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਦੇਵਰਾਜ ਇੰਦਰ ਵੀ ਡੋਲ ਗਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਿਗੇ ਪਬ ਸਰਬੰ ਸ੍ਰਜੇ ਸੁਭ ਸਾਜੰ।","roman":"Dige pab sarban sraje subh saajan |","meaning_en":"all the mountains shook as he put on his fine array;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਡਿਗੇ: 'fell/shook'.","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਪਰਬਤ ਡਿਗ ਪਏ ਸਨ। (ਉਸ ਦੈਂਤ ਨੇ) ਚੰਗੀ ਤਰ੍ਹਾ ਸੈਨਿਕ ਸਾਜ ਸਜਾਇਆ ਹੋਇਆ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਰੇ ਹੂਹ ਦੈ ਕੈ ਭਰੇ ਲੋਹ ਕ੍ਰੋਹੰ।","roman":"Pare hooh dai kai bhare loh krohan |","meaning_en":"they fell on with a shout, filled with the fury of steel,","page":228,"flags":[{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਹ) ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਨਾਲ ਲਾਲ ਹੋਏ ਹੂ-ਹਾ ਕਰਦੇ (ਇੰਜ ਲਗ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ)","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨੋ ਮੇਰ ਕੋ ਸਾਤਵੋ ਸ੍ਰਿੰਗ ਸੋਹੰ। ੨। ੧੫੮।","roman":"Mano mer ko saatvo sring sohan | 2 | 158 |","meaning_en":"as if the seventh peak of Mount Meru stood splendid. 2. 158.","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਨੋ ਸੁਮੇਰ ਪਰਬਤ ਦੀ ਸੱਤਵੀਂ ਚੋਟੀ ਹੋਵੇ ॥੨॥੧੫੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[3,159],"number_text":"੩। ੧੫੯।","page":228,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਜਿਯੋ ਸੈਨ ਸੁਭੰ ਕੀਯੋ ਨਾਦ ਉਚੰ।","roman":"Sajiyo sain subhan keeyo naad uchan |","meaning_en":"He arrayed his fine army and raised a loud cry;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਭੰ: 'fine' or 'Sumbh'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸੁੰਭ ਨੇ ਸੈਨਾ ਸਜਾਈ ਅਤੇ ਉੱਚਾ ਨਾਦ ਕੀਤਾ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਣੈ ਗਰਭਣੀਆਨ ਕੇ ਗਰਭ ਮੁਚੰ।","roman":"Sunai garabhneeaan ke garabh muchan |","meaning_en":"hearing it, pregnant women miscarried;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਜਿਸ ਨੂੰ) ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਗਰਭਿਤ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਦੇ ਗਰਭ-ਪਾਤ ਹੋ ਗਏ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਰਿਯੋ ਲੋਹ ਕ੍ਰੋਹੰ ਉਠੀ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਝਾਰੰ।","roman":"Pariyo loh krohan uthee sasatr jhaaran |","meaning_en":"the fury of steel fell, and weapons clashed;","page":228,"flags":[{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰੋਧਵਾਨ (ਸ਼ੂਰਵੀਰਾ ਦਾ) ਲੋਹਾ ਖੜਕਣ ਲਗਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰ (ਦੇ ਵਜਣ ਨਾਲ) ਚਿੰਗਾਰੀਆਂ ਉਠਣ ਲਗੀਆਂ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਵੀ ਚਾਵਡੀ ਡਾਕਣੀਯੰ ਡਕਾਰੰ। ੩। ੧੫੯।","roman":"Chavee chaavdee daakneeyan dakaaran | 3 | 159 |","meaning_en":"on all four sides the dakinis howled. 3. 159.","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੁੜੇਲਾ ਬੋਲ ਰਹੀਆਂ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਡਾਕਣੀਆਂ ਡਕਾਰ ਰਹੀਆਂ ਸਨ ॥੩॥੧੫੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[4,160],"number_text":"੪। ੧੬੦।","page":228,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੇ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਅਸਤ੍ਰੰ ਕਟੇ ਚਰਮ ਬਰਮੰ।","roman":"Bahe sasatr astran kate charam barman |","meaning_en":"Weapons and missiles struck; shields and armour were cut;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਅਤੇ ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰ ਚਲ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਢਾਲਾ ਤੇ ਕਵਚ ('ਬਰਮੰ') ਕਟੇ ਜਾ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੇ ਕੈ ਨਿਬਾਹਿਯੋ ਭਟੰ ਸੁਆਮਿ ਧਰਮੰ।","roman":"Bhale kai nibaahiyo bhatan suaami dharman |","meaning_en":"the warriors fulfilled their duty to their lord well;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਆਮਿ ਧਰਮੰ: loyalty to one's master.","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਮੇ ਸੁਆਮੀ-ਧਰਮ ਨੂੰ ਚੰਗੀ ਤਰ੍ਹਾ ਨਿਭਾ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠੀ ਕੂਹ ਜੂਹੰ ਗਿਰੇ ਚਉਰ ਚੀਰੰ।","roman":"Uthee kooh joohan gire chaur cheeran |","meaning_en":"cries rose from the hosts; fly-whisks and garments fell;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੂਹ ਜੂਹੰ: 'cries of the multitudes'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿਚ ਸ਼ੋਰ ਮਚ ਗਿਆ ਸੀ ਅਤੇ ਚੌਰ ਅਤੇ ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਡਿਗ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੁਲੇ ਤਛ ਮੁਛੰ ਪਰੀ ਗਛ ਤੀਰੰ। ੪। ੧੬੦।","roman":"Rule tachh muchhan paree gachh teeran | 4 | 160 |","meaning_en":"the hacked and mangled rolled about, as arrows fell in sheaves. 4. 160.","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਛ ਤੀਰੰ: read as 'clusters of arrows'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਵੱਢੇ ਟੁੱਕੇ (ਸ਼ਰੀਰ) ਰੁਲ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਤੀਰਾ ਦੀ ਬੌਛਾੜ ਹੋ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ ॥੪॥੧੬੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[5,161],"number_text":"੫। ੧੬੧।","page":228,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰੇ ਅੰਕੁਸੰ ਬਾਰੁਣੰ ਬੀਰ ਖੇਤੰ।","roman":"Gire ankusan baarunan beer khetan |","meaning_en":"On the battlefield fell elephant-goads and elephants;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿਚ ਅੰਕੁਸ਼, ਹਾਥੀ ('ਬਾਰਣੰ') ਅਤੇ ਸੂਰਵੀਰ ਡਿਗ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਚੇ ਕੰਧ ਹੀਣੰ ਕਬੰਧੰ ਅਚੇਤੰ।","roman":"Nache kandh heenan kabandhan achetan |","meaning_en":"headless trunks danced, senseless;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮੋਢਿਆਂ ਤੋਂ ਬਿਨਾ ਧੜ ਅਚੇਤ ਨਚ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਡੈ ਗ੍ਰਿਧ ਬ੍ਰਿਧੰ ਰੜੈ ਕੰਕ ਬੰਕੰ।","roman":"Udai gridh bridhan rarai kank bankan |","meaning_en":"old vultures flew, crooked herons screeched;","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੱਡੀਆਂ ਗਿੱਧਾ ਉਡ ਰਹੀਆਂ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਕਾ ਸ਼ੋਰ ਪਾ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਕਾ ਭੁੰਕ ਭੇਰੀ ਡਾਹ ਡੂਹ ਡੰਕੰ। ੫। ੧੬੧।","roman":"Bhakaa bhunk bheree daah dooh dankan | 5 | 161 |","meaning_en":"trumpets boomed and drums beat. 5. 161.","page":228,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sound-words.","meaning_pa":"ਭੇਰੀਆਂ ਤੋਂ ਭਕ-ਭਕ ਅਤੇ ਡਗਿਆਂ ਤੋਂ ਡਹਿ-ਡਹਿ ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਨਿਕਲ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ ॥੫॥੧੬੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[6,162],"number_text":"੬। ੧੬੨।","page":229,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਟਕਾ ਟੁਕ ਟੋਪੰ ਢਕਾ ਢੁਕ ਢਾਲੰ।","roman":"Takaa tuk topan dhakaa dhuk dhaalan |","meaning_en":"Helmets clanged, shields were struck;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sound-words.","meaning_pa":"ਟਕ-ਟਕ ਟੋਪਾ ਦੀ, ਢਕ-ਢਕ ਢਾਲਾ ਦੀ (ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਆ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ)","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਛਾ ਮੁਛ ਤੇਗੰ ਬਕੇ ਬਿਕਰਾਲੰ।","roman":"Tachhaa muchh tegan bake bikraalan |","meaning_en":"swords hacked, and the fearsome ones shouted;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਸ਼ਬਦ ਕਰਦੀਆਂ ਹੋਈਆਂ ਵਢਾ-ਟੁਕੀ ਕਰ ਰਹੀਆਂ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਲਾ ਚਾਲ ਬੀਰੰ ਧਮਾ ਧੰਮਿ ਸਾਂਗੰ।","roman":"Halaa chaal beeran dhamaa dhanmi saangan |","meaning_en":"warriors surged to and fro; lances thudded;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਲਾ ਚਾਲ: 'commotion'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਰੀ ਹਾਲ ਹੂਲੰ ਸੁਣਿਯੋ ਲੋਗ ਨਾਗੰ। ੬। ੧੬੨।","roman":"Paree haal hoolan suniyo log naagan | 6 | 162 |","meaning_en":"such an uproar arose that people and serpents (in the netherworld) heard it. 6. 162.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੀਰ ਯੋਧਿਆ ਵਿਚ ਹਿਲ ਜੁਲ ਹੋ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ ਅਤੇ ਬਰਛਿਆਂ (ਦੇ ਲਗਣ ਨਾਲ) ਧੰਮ ਧੰਮ (ਦੀ ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਨਿਕਲ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ)। ਇਤਨਾ ਹਲਾ-ਗੁਲਾ ਹੋ ਰਿਹਾ ਸੀ ਕਿ ਪਾਤਾਲ (ਨਾਗ ਲੋਕ) ਵਿਚ ਸੁਣਾਈ ਪੈ ਰਿਹਾ ਸੀ ॥੬॥੧੬੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB","note_pa":"ਇਹ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਪੰਕਤੀ ਸਮੇਤ ਉੱਪਰਲੀਆਂ 2 ਪੰਕਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[7,163],"number_text":"੭।੧੬੩।","page":229,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਡਕੀ ਡਾਗਣੀ ਜੋਗਣੀਯੰ ਬਿਤਾਲੰ।","roman":"Dakee daagnee jogneeyan bitaalan |","meaning_en":"The dakinis, yoginis and vetals howled;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਡਾਗਣੀ: read as dakini; printed so.","meaning_pa":"ਡਾਕਣੀਆਂ, ਜੋਗਣਾ ਅਤੇ ਬੈਤਾਲ ਬੋਲਦੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਚੇ ਕੰਧ ਹੀਣੰ ਕਬੰਧੰ ਕਪਾਲੰ।","roman":"Nache kandh heenan kabandhan kapaalan |","meaning_en":"headless trunks and skulls danced;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਿਨਾ ਸਿਰ ਅਤੇ ਮੋਢਿਆਂ ਦੇ ਧੜ ਨਚ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਸੇ ਦੇਵ ਸਰਬੰ ਰਿਸ੍ਯੋ ਦਾਨਵੇਸੰ।","roman":"Hase dev sarban risyo daanvesan |","meaning_en":"all the gods laughed, and the demon lord grew angry,","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਧੋ ਅਗਨਿ ਜੁਆਲੰ ਭਯੋ ਆਪ ਭੇਸੰ। ੭।੧੬੩।","roman":"Kidho agni juaalan bhayo aap bhesan | 7 | 163 |","meaning_en":"as if he himself had taken the form of a blazing fire. 7. 163.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਦੇਵਤੇ ਹਸ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਦੈਂਤ ਰਾਜਾ ਕ੍ਰੋਧਵਾਨ ਹੋ ਰਿਹਾ ਸੀ, ਮਾਨੋ ਉਸ ਦਾ ਸਰੂਪ ਅਗਨੀ ਦੀ ਲਾਟ ਵਰਗਾ ਹੋਵੇ ॥੭॥੧੬੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB","note_pa":"ਇਹ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਪੰਕਤੀ ਸਮੇਤ ਉੱਪਰਲੀਆਂ 2 ਪੰਕਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[8,164],"number_text":"੮। ੧੬੪।","page":229,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁੰਭਾਸੁਰ ਜੇਤਿਕੁ ਅਸੁਰ ਪਠਏ ਕੋਪੁ ਬਢਾਇ।","roman":"Sunbhaasur jetiku asur pathae kopu badhaai |","meaning_en":"All the demons whom Sumbhasur sent, his anger growing,","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੁੰਭ ਦੈਂਤ ਨੇ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਵਧਾ ਕੇ ਜਿਤਨੇ ਵੀ ਦੈਂਤ (ਯੁੱਧ-ਭੂਮੀ) ਵਿਚ ਭੇਜੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇ ਦੇਬੀ ਸੋਖਤ ਕਰੇ ਬੂੰਦ ਤਵਾ ਕੀ ਨਿਆਇ। ੮। ੧੬੪।","roman":"Te debee sokhat kare boond tavaa kee niaai | 8 | 164 |","meaning_en":"the goddess dried up like a drop of water on a hot griddle. 8. 164.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਵਾ: an iron griddle.","meaning_pa":"ਉਨ੍ਹਾ ਨੂੰ ਦੇਵੀ ਨੇ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾ ਨਸ਼ਟ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਜਿਵੇਾਂ ਤੱਤੇ ਤਵੇ ਉਤੇ ਪੈਂਦਿਆਂ (ਪਾਣੀ ਦੀ) ਬੂੰਦ ਸੁਕ ਜਾਦੀ ਹੈ ॥੮॥੧੬੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Naraaj chhand","meaning_en":"Naraj metre.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[9,165],"number_text":"੯। ੧੬੫।","page":229,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਬੀਰ ਸੈਣ ਸਜਿ ਕੈ। ਚੜਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਕੋਪ ਗਜਿ ਕੈ।","roman":"Su beer sain saji kai | chariyo su kop gaji kai |","meaning_en":"Arraying his army of fine warriors, he marched out roaring in anger;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੰਗਿਆਂ ਸੂਰਵੀਰਾ ਦੀ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਸਜਾ ਕੇ, ਪੂਰੇ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਨਾਲ ਗਜਦਾ ਹੋਇਆ (ਸੁੰਭ) ਚੜ੍ਹ ਪਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਧਾਰ ਕੈ। ਪੁਕਾਰ ਮਾਰੁ ਮਾਰ ਕੈ। ੯। ੧੬੫।","roman":"Chaliyo su sasatr dhaar kai | pukaar maaru maar kai | 9 | 165 |","meaning_en":"he went forth bearing his weapons, crying 'Kill! Kill!' 9. 165.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰ ਧਾਰ ਕੇ ਚਲ ਪਿਆ- ਮਾਰੋ' 'ਮਾਰੋ' ਪੁਕਾਰਦਾ ਹੋਇਆ ॥੯॥੧੬੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੰਗੀਤ ਮਧੁਭਾਰ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਸੰਗੀਤ ਮਧੁਭਾਰ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Sangeet madhubhaar chhand","meaning_en":"Sangit Madhubhar metre.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"This metre is built on sound-words (kagarhdang etc.), left untranslated.","meaning_pa":"ਸੰਗੀਤ ਮਧੁਭਾਰ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[10,166],"number_text":"੧੦। ੧੬੬।","page":229,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕੜਾਕ। ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤੜਾਕ।","roman":"Kaagardan karaak | taagardan taraak |","meaning_en":"Crashing and cracking;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sound-words.","meaning_pa":"ਕੜਾਕ-ਕੜਾਕ ਅਤੇ ਤਾੜ-ਤਾੜ ਦੀ ਧੁਨੀ ਹੋ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਗੜਦੰ ਸੁ ਬੀਰ। ਗਾਗੜਦੰ ਗਹੀਰ। ੧੦। ੧੬੬।","roman":"Saagardan su beer | gaagardan gaheer | 10 | 166 |","meaning_en":"the fine warriors, deep-voiced. 10. 166.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sound-words.","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਵੀਰ ਗੜਗੜ ਕਰਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਗਰਜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ॥੧੦॥੧੬੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[11,167],"number_text":"੧੧। ੧੬੭।","page":229,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਗੜਦੰ ਨਿਸਾਣ। ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੁਆਣ।","roman":"Naagardan nisaan | jaagardan juaan |","meaning_en":"The war-drums sound; the young warriors wake;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਨਾਦ ਕਰ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ, ਜੁਆਨ ਜੂਝ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਗੜਦੀ ਨਿਹੰਗ। ਪਾਗੜਦੀ ਪਲੰਗ। ੧੧। ੧੬੭।","roman":"Naagardee nihang | paagardee palang | 11 | 167 |","meaning_en":"the fearless ones, and the leopard-like warriors. 11. 167.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਿਹੰਗ: 'fearless warriors'; ਪਲੰਗ: 'leopard'.","meaning_pa":"ਮਗਰਮੱਛਾ ('ਨਿਹੰਗ') ਵਾਗ ਇਕ ਦੂਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਪਕੜਦੇ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਚਿਤਰਿਆਂ ਵਾਗ ਉਛਲ ਕੇ ਪੈਂਦੇ ਸਨ ॥੧੧॥੧੬੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[12,168],"number_text":"੧੨। ੧੬੮।","page":229,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਗੜਦੀ ਤਮਕਿ। ਲਾਗੜਦੀ ਲਹਕਿ।","roman":"Taagardee tamki | laagardee lahki |","meaning_en":"They flare up in rage, they surge forward;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਗੁੱਸੇ ਨਾਲ ਤਾੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਦਗ-ਦਗ ਕਰੇ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ। ਬਾਹੈ ਜੁਆਣ। ੧੨। ੧੬੮।","roman":"Kaagardan kripaan | baahai juaan | 12 | 168 |","meaning_en":"the young warriors swing their swords. 12. 168.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਵੀਰ ਕਠੋਰ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨਾ ਨੂੰ ਚਲਾ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ॥੧੨॥੧੬੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[13,169],"number_text":"੧੩। ੧੬੯।","page":229,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖਾਗੜਦੀ ਖਤੰਗ। ਨਾਗੜਦੀ ਨਿਹੰਗ।","roman":"Khaagardee khatang | naagardee nihang |","meaning_en":"Arrows, fearless warriors;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਖਰ-ਖਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਤੀਰ ('ਖਤੰਗ') ਸੂਰਮਿਆਂ (ਨਿਹੰਗਾ) ਨੇ ਫੜੇ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛਾਗੜਦੀ ਛੁਟੰਤ। ਆਗੜਦੀ ਉਡੰਤ। ੧੩। ੧੬੯।","roman":"Chhaagardee chhutant | aagardee udant | 13 | 169 |","meaning_en":"they are loosed and they fly. 13. 169.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਛੜ-ਛੜ ਕਰਦੇ ਛੁਟਦੇ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਅਗੋਂ ਆਣ ਵਾਲਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਉਡਾਉਾਂਦੇ ਜਾਦੇ ਸਨ ॥੧੩॥੧੬੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[14,170],"number_text":"੧੪। ੧੭੦।","page":229,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਗੜਦੀ ਪਵੰਗ। ਸਾਗੜਦੀ ਸੁਭੰਗ।","roman":"Paagardee pavang | saagardee subhang |","meaning_en":"Horses, well-adorned;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਭੰਗ: read as 'fine, handsome'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਪਗੜੀਆਂ ਵਾਲੇ (ਯੋਧੇ) ਘੋੜੇ ('ਪਵੰਗ') ਅਤੇ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਅੰਗਾ ਵਾਲੇ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਗੜਦੀ ਜੁਆਣ। ਝਾਗੜਦੀ ਜੁਝਾਣਿ। ੧੪। ੧੭੦।","roman":"Jaagardee juaan | jhaagardee jujhaani | 14 | 170 |","meaning_en":"young warriors, fighting fiercely. 14. 170.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜੁਝਾਣਿ: 'fighting'.","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਮੇ ਜਗਹ ਜਗਹ ਉਤੇ ਜੁਆਨ ਝਗੜਦੇ ਅਤੇ ਜੂਝਦੇ ਸਨ ॥੧੪॥੧੭੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[15,171],"number_text":"੧੫। ੧੭੧।","page":229,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਝਾਗੜਦੀ ਝੜੰਗ। ਕਾਗੜਦੀ ਕੜੰਗ।","roman":"Jhaagardee jharang | kaagardee karang |","meaning_en":"Clanging and clashing;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sound-words.","meaning_pa":"ਝੜ-ਝੜ ਕਰਦੇ ਝੜਦੇ ਸਨ, ਕੜ-ਕੜ ਕਰਦੇ ਕੜਕਦੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਗੜਦੀ ਤੜਾਕ। ਚਾਗੜਦੀ ਚਟਾਕ। ੧੫। ੧੭੧।","roman":"Taagardee taraak | chaagardee chataak | 15 | 171 |","meaning_en":"cracking and snapping. 15. 171.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sound-words.","meaning_pa":"ਤੜ-ਤੜ ਕਰਦੇ (ਗੋਲੇ) ਨਿਕਲਦੇ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਚੜਚੜ ਕਰਦੇ (ਬਰਛੇ) ਵਜਦੇ ਸਨ ॥੧੫॥੧੭੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[16,172],"number_text":"੧੬। ੧੭੨।","page":229,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਘਾਗੜਦੀ ਘਬਾਕ। ਭਾਗੜਦੀ ਭਭਾਕ।","roman":"Ghaagardee ghabaak | bhaagardee bhabhaak |","meaning_en":"Gashing and gushing (of wounds);","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਘਬਾਕ, ਭਭਾਕ: sound-words for wounds and blood.","meaning_pa":"ਘੜ-ਘੜ (ਪੇਟ ਵਿਚ ਗੋਲੇ) ਵਜਦੇ ਸਨ, ਭੜ-ਭੜ ਕਰਦੇ (ਜ਼ਖਮਾ ਦੇ) ਮੂੰਹ ਖੁਲਦੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕਪਾਲਿ। ਨਚੀ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਾਲ। ੧੬। ੧੭੨।","roman":"Kaagardan kapaali | nachee bikraal | 16 | 172 |","meaning_en":"Kapali, the fearsome one, danced. 16. 172.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਪਾਲਿ: Kali, bearer of skulls.","meaning_pa":"(ਯੁੱਧ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿਚ) ਕਪਾਲੀ (ਕਾਲਕਾ) ਭਿਆਨਕ ਰੂਪ ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰਕੇ ਨਚ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ ॥੧੬॥੧੭੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Naraaj chhand","meaning_en":"Naraj metre.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[17,173],"number_text":"੧੭। ੧੭੩।","page":229,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਨੰਤ ਦੁਸਟ ਮਾਰੀਯੰ। ਬਿਅੰਤ ਸੋਕ ਟਾਰੀਯੰ।","roman":"Anant dusat maareeyan | biant sok taareeyan |","meaning_en":"She killed countless wicked ones and removed endless sorrow;","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਨੰਤ ਦੁਸ਼ਟਾ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰ ਕੇ (ਦੁਰਗਾ ਨੇ) ਬੇਅੰਤ ਦੁਖ ਦੂਰ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਮੰਧ ਅੰਧ ਉਠੀਯੰ। ਬਿਸੇਖ ਬਾਣ ਬੁਠੀਯੰ। ੧੭। ੧੭੩।","roman":"Kamandh andh utheeyan | bisekh baan butheeyan | 17 | 173 |","meaning_en":"blind headless trunks rose up; arrows rained down especially. 17. 173.","page":229,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੰਨ੍ਹੇ ਵਾਹ ਧੜ ਉਠ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਵਿਸ਼ੇਸ਼ ਢੰਗ ਨਾਲ ਤੀਰ ਚਲਾਉਾਂਦੇ ਸਨ ॥੧੭॥੧੭੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[18,174],"number_text":"੧੮। ੧੭੪।","page":230,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੜਕਾ ਕਰਮੁਕੰ ਉਧੰ। ਸੜਾਕ ਸੈਹਥੀ ਜੁਧੰ।","roman":"Karkaa karmukan udhan | saraak saihthee judhan |","meaning_en":"Bows twanged, raised high; spears hissed in the battle;","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਰਮੁਕੰ: bow (karmuk).","meaning_pa":"ਧਨੁਸਾ ('ਕਰਮੁਕੰ') ਦੀ ਕੜਾਕ-ਕੜਾਕ ਦੀ ਉੱਚੀ ਧੁਨੀ ਅਤੇ ਸੜ-ਸੜ ਕਰਦੀਆਂ ਸੈਹੱਥੀਆਂ ਦੀ ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਹੋ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਅੰਤ ਬਾਣਿ ਬਰਖਯੰ। ਬਿਸੇਖ ਬੀਰ ਪਰਖਯੰ। ੧੮। ੧੭੪।","roman":"Biant baani barakhyan | bisekh beer parakhyan | 18 | 174 |","meaning_en":"countless arrows rained down; the warriors were especially tested. 18. 174.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬੇਅੰਤ (ਸੂਰਮੇ) ਬਾਣਾ ਦੀ ਬਰਖਾ ਕਰਦੇ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਵਿਸ਼ੇਸ਼ ਸੂਰਮਿਆਂ ਦੀ ਪਰਖ ਹੋ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ ॥੧੮॥੧੭੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੰਗੀਤ ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਸੰਗੀਤ ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Sangeet naraaj chhand","meaning_en":"Sangit Naraj metre.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੰਗੀਤ ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[19,175],"number_text":"੧੯।੧੭੫।","page":230,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੜਾ ਕੜੀ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣਯੰ।","roman":"Karaa karee kripaanyan |","meaning_en":"Swords clash,","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sound-words.","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨਾ ਦੀ ਕੜ-ਕੜ ਦੀ (ਆਵਾਜ਼) ਹੁੰਦੀ ਸੀ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਟਾ ਜੁਟੀ ਜੁਆਣਯੰ।","roman":"Jataa jutee juaanyan |","meaning_en":"young warriors grapple by the matted hair;","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਟਾ ਜੁਟੀ: 'locked by the hair', i.e. closely grappling; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਜੁਆਨ (ਇਕ-ਦੂਜੇ ਨਾਲ) ਗੁਥਮ ਗੁਥਾ ਹੋ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਬੀਰ ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜਗੇ।","roman":"Subeer jaagardan jage |","meaning_en":"the fine warriors are roused,","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਵੀਰ ਉਤੇਜਿਤ ਸਨ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲੜਾਕ ਲਾਗੜਦੰ ਪਗੇ। ੧੯।੧੭੫।","roman":"Laraak laagardan page | 19 | 175 |","meaning_en":"the fighters are steeped (in battle). 19. 175.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਗੇ: 'absorbed, steeped'.","meaning_pa":"ਅਤੇ ਲੜਾਕਿਆਂ ਨਾਲ ਆ ਕੇ ਲੜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ॥੧੯॥੧੭੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"Rasaval metre.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[20,176],"number_text":"੨੦। ੧੭੬।","page":230,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਝਮੀ ਤੇਗ ਝਟੰ। ਛੁਰੀ ਛਿਪ੍ਰ ਛੁਟੰ।","roman":"Jhamee teg jhatan | chhuree chhipr chhutan |","meaning_en":"Swords flash swiftly; knives are loosed quickly;","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਛਿਪ੍ਰ: 'quick' (kshipra).","meaning_pa":"(ਸੂਰਮੇ) ਝਟ-ਪਟ ਤੇਗਾ ਚਮਕਾਉਾਂਦੇ ਸਨ, ਛੁਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਤੇਜ਼ੀ ਨਾਲ ਚਲਾਉਾਂਦੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗੁਰੰ ਗੁਰਜ ਗਟੰ। ਪਲੰਗੰ ਪਿਸਟੰ। ੨੦। ੧੭੬।","roman":"Guran guraj gatan | palangan pistan | 20 | 176 |","meaning_en":"maces strike heavily; leopard-like warriors are crushed. 20. 176.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਲੰਗੰ ਪਿਸਟੰ: 'warriors (leopards) ground down'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਭਾਰੀ (ਗੁਰੰ) ਗੁਰਜਾ ਨੂੰ ਗਟ-ਗਟ ਕਰਦੇ ਸ਼ੇਰ ਦੀ ਪਿਠ ਉਤੇ ਮਾਰਦੇ ਸਨ ॥੨੦॥੧੭੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[21,177],"number_text":"੨੧। ੧੭੭।","page":230,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਸ੍ਰੋਣ ਚਟੰ। ਕਿਤੇ ਸੀਸ ਫੁਟੰ।","roman":"Kite sron chatan | kite sees phutan |","meaning_en":"Some lick up blood, some heads are split;","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ (ਗਿਦੜ ਆਦਿ ਸੂਰਮਿਆਂ ਦਾ) ਲਹੂ ਚਟ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ, ਕਿਤੇ ਸਿਰ ਫੁਟੇ ਪਏ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਹੂਹ ਛੁਟੰ। ਕਹੂੰ ਬੀਰ ਉਠੰ। ੨੧। ੧੭੭।","roman":"Kahoon hooh chhutan | kahoon beer uthan | 21 | 177 |","meaning_en":"here cries burst out, there warriors rise. 21. 177.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਹਲਾ-ਗੁਲਾ ਹੋ ਰਿਹਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਕਿਤੇ ਵੀਰ ਯੋਧੇ ਫਿਰ ਉਠ ਖੜੋਤੇ ਸਨ ॥੨੧॥੧੭੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[22,178],"number_text":"੨੨। ੧੭੮।","page":230,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਧੂਰਿ ਲੁਟੰ। ਕਿਤੇ ਮਾਰ ਰਟੰ।","roman":"Kahoon dhoori lutan | kite maar ratan |","meaning_en":"Here some roll in the dust, there some cry 'Kill!';","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ (ਸੂਰਮੇ) ਧੂੜ ਵਿਚ ਲੇਟੇ ਪਏ ਸਨ, ਕਿਤੇ ਮਾਰੋ-ਮਾਰੋ ਬੋਲ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਣੈ ਜਸ ਭਟੰ। ਕਿਤੇ ਪੇਟ ਫਟੰ। ੨੨। ੧੭੮।","roman":"Bhanai jas bhatan | kite pet phatan | 22 | 178 |","meaning_en":"bards sing of glory; some bellies are ripped open. 22. 178.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਟੰ: here 'bards' (bhatt) or 'warriors'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਭੱਟ ਲੋਕ ਯਸ਼ ਗਾ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਕਿਤੇ ਪਾਟੇ ਹੋਏ ਪੇਟ ਪਏ ਸਨ ॥੨੨॥੧੭੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[23,179],"number_text":"੨੩। ੧੭੯।","page":230,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਜੇ ਛਤ੍ਰਿ ਥਟੰ। ਕਿਤੇ ਖੂਨ ਖਟੰ।","roman":"Bhaje chhatri thatan | kite khoon khatan |","meaning_en":"The hosts of Kshatriyas flee; some are soaked in blood;","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖੂਨ ਖਟੰ: read as 'earn/are covered with blood'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਛਤਰਾ ਨੂੰ ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲੇ ਭਜੇ ਜਾਦੇ ਸਨ, ਕਿਤੇ ਖੂਨ ਵਹਾਇਆ ਜਾ ਰਿਹਾ ਸੀ ('ਖਟੰ')","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਦੁਸਟ ਦਟੰ। ਫਿਰੇ ਜ੍ਯੋ ਹਰਟੰ। ੨੩। ੧੭੯।","roman":"Kite dusat datan | phire jyo hartan | 23 | 179 |","meaning_en":"some wicked ones are pressed down; they turn like a Persian wheel. 23. 179.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਰਟੰ: a Persian water-wheel.","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਦੁਸ਼ਟਾ ਨੂੰ ਨਸ਼ਟ ਕੀਤਾ ਜਾ ਰਿਹਾ ਸੀ ਅਤੇ ਕਿਤੇ (ਵੀਰ ਯੋਧੇ) ਹਰਟ ਵਾਗ ਫਿਰ ਰਹੇ ਹਨ ॥੨੩॥੧੭੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[24,180],"number_text":"੨੪। ੧੮੦।","page":230,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਜੇ ਸੂਰ ਸਾਰੇ। ਮਹਿਖੁਆਸ ਧਾਰੇ।","roman":"Saje soor saare | mahikhuaas dhaare |","meaning_en":"All the warriors are armed; they hold their bows;","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਸੂਰਵੀਰ ਸਜੇ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ, (ਹੱਥ ਵਿਚ) ਧਨੁਸ਼ ('ਮਹਿਖੁਆਸ') ਧਾਰੇ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਏ ਖਗਆਰੇ। ਮਹਾ ਰੋਹ ਵਾਰੇ। ੨੪। ੧੮੦।","roman":"Lae khaga'aare | mahaa roh vaare | 24 | 180 |","meaning_en":"they take up swords, those of great wrath. 24. 180.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖਗਆਰੇ: 'swords' (kharag).","meaning_pa":"(ਹੱਥ ਵਿਚ) ਤਿਖੇ ਖੰਡੇ ਲਏ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਵਾਲੇ ਸਨ ॥੨੪॥੧੮੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[25,181],"number_text":"੨੫। ੧੮੧।","page":230,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਹੀ ਰੂਪ ਕਾਰੇ। ਮਨੋ ਸਿੰਧੁ ਖਾਰੇ।","roman":"Sahee roop kaare | mano sindhu khaare |","meaning_en":"Truly black in form, like the salt ocean,","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਹ) ਠੀਕ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾ ਦੇ ਕਾਲੇ ਸਨ ਮਾਨੋ ਖਾਰਾ ਸਮੁੰਦਰ ਹੋਵੇ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਈ ਬਾਰ ਗਾਰੀ। ਸੁ ਮਾਰੰ ਉਚਾਰੇ। ੨੫। ੧੮੧।","roman":"Kaee baar gaaree | su maaran uchaare | 25 | 181 |","meaning_en":"many times they utter abuse, and cry 'Kill!'. 25. 181.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਭਾਵੇਾਂ ਦੁਰਗਾ ਨੇ ਉਨ੍ਹਾ ਨੂੰ) ਕਈ ਵਾਰ ਨਸ਼ਟ ਕੀਤਾ ਸੀ (ਪਰ ਉਹ ਫਿਰ ਵੀ) ਮਾਰੋ-ਮਾਰੋ ਪੁਕਾਰਦੇ ਸਨ ॥੨੫॥੧੮੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[26,182],"number_text":"੨੬। ੧੮੨।","page":230,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਵਾਨੀ ਪਛਾਰੇ। ਜਵਾ ਜੇਮਿ ਜਾਰੇ।","roman":"Bhavaanee pachhaare | javaa jemi jaare |","meaning_en":"Bhavani struck them down, burning them like barley;","page":230,"flags":[{"code":"ੇੇ","reason":"same sign typed twice; written once (prints as one)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਵਾ: 'barley'; ਜੇਮਿ: 'like'.","meaning_pa":"ਭਵਾਨੀ ਨੇ (ਉਨ੍ਹਾ ਨੂੰ) ਪਛਾੜ ਦਿੱਤਾ, ਜਿਵੇਾਂ ਜਵਾਹੇ ਨੂੰ (ਚੌਮਾਸੇ ਦੀ ਬਰਖਾ) ਸਾੜ ਦਿੰਦੀ ਹੈ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਡੇਈ ਲੁਝਾਰੇ। ਹੁਤੇ ਜੇ ਹੀਏ ਵਾਰੇ। ੨੬। ੧੮੨।","roman":"Bade'ee lujhaare | hute je hee'e vaare | 26 | 182 |","meaning_en":"great fighters, those who were brave of heart. 26. 182.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਲੁਝਾਰੇ: read as 'fighters' (jujhare).","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਹੜੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਲੜਾਕੇ ਅਤੇ ਤਕੜੇ ਹੌਂਸਲੇ ਵਾਲੇ ਸਨ ॥੨੬॥੧੮੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[27,183],"number_text":"੨੭। ੧੮੩।","page":230,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਕੰ ਬਾਰ ਟਾਰੇ। ਠਮੰ ਠੋਕਿ ਠਾਰੇ।","roman":"Ikan baar taare | thaman thoki thaare |","meaning_en":"At one stroke she removed them; she struck and laid them low;","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਠਮੰ ਠੋਕਿ ਠਾਰੇ: 'struck them firm and still'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਦੇਵੀ ਨੇ ਦੈਂਤ ਵੀਰਾ ਨੂੰ) ਇਕ ਵਾਰ ਤਾ ਉਖਾੜ ਸੁਟਿਆ ਸੀ ਅਤੇ ਮਾਰ-ਮਾਰ ਕੇ ਠੰਡਾ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਲੀ ਮਾਰ ਡਾਰੇ। ਢਮਕੇ ਢਢਾਰੇ। ੨੭। ੧੮੩।","roman":"Balee maar daare | dhamke dhadhaare | 27 | 183 |","meaning_en":"she killed the mighty ones; drums boomed. 27. 183.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਢਢਾਰੇ: a kind of drum; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਬੜੇ ਬੜੇ) ਬਲਵਾਨਾ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਸੀ। ਢੱਢਾ ਦੀ ਢੰਮ ਢੰਮ ਦੀ (ਧੁਨੀ ਲਗਾਤਾਰ ਹੋ ਰਹੀ ਹੈ) ॥੨੭॥੧੮੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[28,184],"number_text":"੨੮।੧੮੪।","page":230,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੇ ਬਾਣਣਿਆਰੇ। ਕਿਤੈ ਤੀਰ ਤਾਰੇ।","roman":"Bahe baanniaare | kitai teer taare |","meaning_en":"The archers shot; some arrows passed right through;","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਣਣਿਆਰੇ: 'arrow-shooters'; ਤਾਰੇ: 'sent across'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਅਣੀਆਰੇ ਤੀਰ ਚਲਦੇ ਸਨ, (ਉਨ੍ਹਾ) ਤੀਰਾ ਨੇ ਕਿਤਨੇ (ਯੁੱਧਵੀਰ) (ਯੁੱਧ ਰੂਪੀ ਨਦੀ ਤੋਂ) ਪਾਰ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਖੇ ਹਾਥ ਬਾਰੇ। ਦਿਵਾਨੇ ਦਿਦਾਰੇ। ੨੮।੧੮੪।","roman":"Lakhe haath baare | divaane didaare | 28 | 184 |","meaning_en":"they saw her hands' prowess, frenzied at the sight of her. 28. 184.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਾਥ ਬਾਰੇ / ਦਿਵਾਨੇ ਦਿਦਾਰੇ: very uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕਈ ਬਲਵਾਨ ਯੋਧੇ (ਦੇਵੀ ਨੂੰ) ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਸੁੱਧ-ਬੁੱਧ ਭੁਲਾ ਬੈਠੇ ਸਨ ॥੨੮॥੧੮੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[29,185],"number_text":"੨੯। ੧੮੫।","page":230,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਣੇ ਭੂਮਿ ਪਾਰੇ। ਕਿਤੇ ਸਿੰਘ ਫਾਰੇ।","roman":"Hane bhoomi paare | kite singh phaare |","meaning_en":"She slew them and threw them on the ground; the lion tore some apart;","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਦੇਵੀ ਨੇ) ਕਈਆਂ (ਦੈਂਤਾ) ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰ ਕੇ ਭੂਮੀ ਉਤੇ ਪਾ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਅਤੇ ਕਈਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਸ਼ੇਰ ਨੇ ਪਾੜ ਸੁਟਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਆਪੁ ਬਾਰੇ। ਜਿਤੇ ਦੈਤ ਭਾਰੇ। ੨੯। ੧੮੫।","roman":"Kite aapu baare | jite dait bhaare | 29 | 185 |","meaning_en":"some she struck down herself; as many great demons as there were 29. 185.","page":230,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਆਪੁ ਬਾਰੇ: 'she herself struck'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤਨੇ ਹੀ ਵਡੇ ਵਡੇ ਹੰਕਾਰੀ ਦੈਂਤਾ ਨੂੰ (ਦੇਵੀ ਨੇ) ਆਪ ਜਿਤ ਲਿਆ ॥੨੯॥੧੮੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[30,186],"number_text":"੩੦। ੧੮੬।","page":231,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਤੇ ਅੰਤ ਹਾਰੇ। ਬਡੇਈ ਅੜਿਆਰੇ।","roman":"Tite ant haare | bade'ee ariaare |","meaning_en":"all were defeated in the end, great and stubborn ones,","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਸਾਰੇ ਅੰਤ ਨੂੰ ਹਾਰ ਗਏ ਜਿਹੜੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਅੜੀਅਲ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖਰੇਈ ਬਰਿਆਰੇ। ਕਰੂਰੰ ਕਰਾਰੇ। ੩੦। ੧੮੬।","roman":"Khare'ee bariaare | karooran karaare | 30 | 186 |","meaning_en":"truly mighty, cruel and fierce. 30. 186.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਖਰੂਦੀ ਅਤੇ ਧਕਾ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲੇ ਸਨ, ਕਠੋਰ ਅਤੇ ਜ਼ਾਲਮ ਸਨ ॥੩੦॥੧੮੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[31,187],"number_text":"੩੧। ੧੮੭।","page":231,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਪਕੇ ਲਲਾਹੇ। ਅਰੀਲੇ ਅਰਿਆਰੇ।","roman":"Lapke lalaahe | areele ariaare |","meaning_en":"They sprang forward eagerly, the stubborn, resisting foes;","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਲਲਾਹੇ / ਅਰੀਲੇ ਅਰਿਆਰੇ: read as 'eager' and 'obstinate'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਜਿਨ੍ਹਾ ਦੇ) ਮੱਥੇ ਚਮਕਦੇ ਸਨ, ਅੜੀਅਲ ਅਤੇ ਆਕੜਖਾਨ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਣੇ ਕਾਲ ਕਾਰੇ। ਭਜੇ ਰੋਹ ਵਾਰੇ। ੩੧। ੧੮੭।","roman":"Hane kaal kaare | bhaje roh vaare | 31 | 187 |","meaning_en":"the black Kali slew them, and the wrathful ones fled. 31. 187.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਲ ਕਾਰੇ: read as 'black Kal/Kali'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਉਨ੍ਹਾ) ਕਾਲਿਆਂ (ਦੈਂਤਾ) ਨੂੰ ਕਾਲਕਾ ਨੇ ਮਾਰ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਅਤੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲੇ (ਰਣਭੂਮੀ ਵਿਚੋਂ) ਭਜ ਗਏ ॥੩੧॥੧੮੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[32,188],"number_text":"੩੨। ੧੮੮।","page":231,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਬਿਧਿ ਦੁਸਟ ਪ੍ਰਜਾਰ ਕੈ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਕਰਿ ਲੀਨ।","roman":"Ih bidhi dusat prajaar kai sasatr asatr kari leen |","meaning_en":"Having burned up the wicked in this way, she took weapons and missiles in hand;","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾ ਦੁਸ਼ਟਾ ਨੂੰ ਨਸ਼ਟ ਕਰ ਕੇ (ਦੇਵੀ ਨੇ) ਹੱਥ ਵਿਚ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਅਤੇ ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰ ਫੜ ਲਏ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਣ ਬੂੰਦ ਪ੍ਰਿਥਮੈ ਸਿੰਘ ਨਾਦ ਪੁਨਿ ਕੀਨ। ੩੨। ੧੮੮।","roman":"Baan boond prithmai singh naad puni keen | 32 | 188 |","meaning_en":"first she rained drops of arrows, then she roared like a lion. 32. 188.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"Rasaval metre.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪਹਿਲਾ (ਬਰਖਾ ਦੀਆਂ) ਬੂੰਦਾ ਵਾਗ ਬਾਣਾ (ਦੀ ਵਾਛੜ ਲਾਈ) ਅਤੇ ਫਿਰ ਸਿੰਘ-ਨਾਦ ਕੀਤਾ ॥੩੨॥੧੮੮॥ ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB","note_pa":"ਇਹ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਪੰਕਤੀ ਸਮੇਤ ਉੱਪਰਲੀਆਂ 2 ਪੰਕਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਹੈ।"},{"type":"verse","number":[33,189],"number_text":"੩੩। ੧੮੯।","page":231,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਣਿਯੋ ਸੁੰਭ ਰਾਯੰ। ਚੜਿਯੋ ਚਉਪ ਚਾਯੰ।","roman":"Suniyo sunbh raayan | chariyo chaup chaayan |","meaning_en":"King Sumbh heard it, and marched out with eager zeal;","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਜਦੋਂ) ਸੁੰਭ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ (ਇਹ) ਸੁਣਿਆ ਤਾ ਬੜੇ ਉਤਸਾਹ ਨਾਲ (ਜੰਗ ਕਰਨ ਲਈ) ਚੜ੍ਹ ਪਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਜੇ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਪਾਣੰ। ਚੜੇ ਜੰਗਿ ਜੁਆਣੰ। ੩੩। ੧੮੯।","roman":"Saje sasatr paanan | chare jangi juaanan | 33 | 189 |","meaning_en":"with weapons in hand, young warriors went out to war. 33. 189.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੱਥਾ ਵਿਚ ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਜਾ ਕੇ (ਦੈਂਤ) ਸੈਨਿਕ ਯੁੱਧ ਲਈ ਨਿਕਲ ਪਏ ॥੩੩॥੧੮੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[34,190],"number_text":"੩੪। ੧੯੦।","page":231,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਗੈ ਢੋਲ ਢੰਕੇ। ਕਮਾਣੰ ਕੜੰਕੇ।","roman":"Lagai dhol dhanke | kamaanan karanke |","meaning_en":"Drums began to beat; bows twanged;","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਢੋਲਾ ਉਤੇ ਡਗੇ ਵਜਣ ਲਗੇ, ਕਮਾਨਾ ਕੜਕਣ ਲਗੀਆਂ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਏ ਨਦ ਨਾਦੰ। ਧੁਣੰ ਨਿਰਬਿਖਾਦੰ। ੩੪। ੧੯੦।","roman":"Bhae nad naadan | dhunan nirbikhaadan | 34 | 190 |","meaning_en":"loud cries arose, the sound clear and undaunted. 34. 190.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਿਰਬਿਖਾਦੰ: as in 1.11.0; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਧੌਂਸਿਆ ਦੇ ਨਾਦ ਹੋਣ ਲਗੇ, (ਅਤੇ ਉਨ੍ਹਾ ਦੀ) ਧੁਨੀ ਲਗਾਤਾਰ ਹੋਣ ਲਗੀ ॥੩੪॥੧੯੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[35,191],"number_text":"੩੫। ੧੯੧।","page":231,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਮਕੀ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣੰ। ਹਠੇ ਤੇਜ ਮਾਣੰ।","roman":"Chamkee kripaanan | hathe tej maanan |","meaning_en":"Swords flashed; the stubborn ones were proud of their might;","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨਾ ਚਮਕ ਰਹੀਆਂ ਸਨ। ਹਠੀ ਯੋਧੇ (ਆਪਣੇ) ਤੇਜ ਉਤੇ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾਬੀਰ ਹੁੰਕੇ। ਸੁ ਨੀਸਾਣ ਦ੍ਰੁੰਕੇ। ੩੫। ੧੯੧।","roman":"Mahaabeer hunke | su neesaan drunke | 35 | 191 |","meaning_en":"great warriors shouted; the war-drums boomed. 35. 191.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਣ ਕਰ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ, ਧੌਂਸਿਆਂ ਦੀ ਗੂੰਜ ਉਠ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ ॥੩੫॥੧੯੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[36,192],"number_text":"੩੬। ੧੯੨।","page":231,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਹੂੰ ਓਰ ਗਰਜੇ। ਸਬੇ ਦੇਵ ਲਰਜੇ।","roman":"Chahoon or garje | sabe dev larje |","meaning_en":"They thundered on all four sides; all the gods trembled;","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਹਾ ਪਾਸਿਆਂ ਤੋਂ (ਦੈਂਤ) ਗਰਜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ, ਸਾਰੇ ਦੇਵਤੇ ਕੰਬ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰੰ ਧਾਰ ਬਰਖੇ। ਮਈਯਾ ਪਾਣ ਪਰਖੇ। ੩੬। ੧੯੨।","roman":"Saran dhaar barkhe | maeeyaa paan parkhe | 36 | 192 |","meaning_en":"they rained streams of arrows; the Mother tested their strength. 36. 192.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਾਣ ਪਰਖੇ: 'tested the hands/strength'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਬਾਣਾ ਦੀ ਬਰਖਾ ਹੋ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ, ਮਾਤਾ ਦੁਰਗਾ ਦੇ ਹੱਥਾ (ਦਾ ਮਜ਼ਾ ਦੈਂਤ) ਚਖ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ॥੩੬॥੧੯੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[37,193],"number_text":"੩੭। ੧੯੩।","page":231,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇ ਲਏ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਾਮੁਹੇ ਧਏ। ਤਿਤੇ ਨਿਧਨ ਕਹੁੰ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤਿ ਭਏ।","roman":"Je lae sasatr saamuhe dhae | tite nidhan kahun praapti bhae |","meaning_en":"All who took weapons and rushed at her met their death;","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਹੜੇ (ਦੈਂਤ) ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰ ਲੈ ਕੇ (ਦੁਰਗਾ ਦੇ) ਸਾਹਮਣੇ ਆਏ, ਉਨ੍ਹਾ (ਸਾਰਿਆਂ ਦੀ) ਮ੍ਰਿਤੂ ਹੋ ਗਈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਝਮਕਤ ਭਈ ਅਸਨ ਕੀ ਧਾਰਾ। ਭਭਕੇ ਰੁੰਡ ਮੁੰਡ ਬਿਕਰਾਰਾ। ੩੭। ੧੯੩।","roman":"Jhamkat bhaee asan kee dhaaraa | bhabhke rund mund bikraaraa | 37 | 193 |","meaning_en":"the edges of swords flashed; trunks and heads, dreadful, gushed blood. 37. 193.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਸਨ: read as 'swords' (asi); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨਾ ('ਅਸਨ') ਦੀ ਧਾਰ ਚਮਕਾ ਮਾਰ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ। ਸਿਰ ਅਤੇ ਧੜ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਢੰਗ ਨਾਲ ਭਬਕ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ॥੩੭॥੧੯੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[38,194],"number_text":"੩੮। ੧੯੪।","page":231,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹੈ ਗੈ ਰਥ ਪੈਦਲ ਕਟੇ ਬਚਿਯੋ ਨ ਜੀਵਤ ਕੋਇ।","roman":"Hai gai rath paidal kate bachiyo na jeevat koi |","meaning_en":"Horses, elephants, chariots and foot-soldiers were cut down; none was left alive;","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਘੋੜੇ, ਹਾਥੀ, ਰਥ ਅਤੇ ਪੈਦਲ (ਚੌਹਾ ਤਰ੍ਹਾ ਦੀ ਸੈਨਾ) ਕਟ ਦਿੱਤੀ ਗਈ ਸੀ (ਉਨ੍ਹਾ ਵਿਚੋਂ) ਕੋਈ ਵੀ ਜਿਉਾਂਦਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਚਿਆ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਆਪੇ ਨਿਕਸਿਯੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਤਿ ਸੁੰਭ ਕਰੈ ਸੋ ਹੋਇ। ੩੮। ੧੯੪।","roman":"Tab aape niksiyo nripti sunbh karai so hoi | 38 | 194 |","meaning_en":"then King Sumbh himself came out; what he does, that comes to be. 38. 194.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਰੈ ਸੋ ਹੋਇ: may refer to Sumbh's might, or mean 'what (God) does, happens'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਤਦ ਦੈਂਤ ਰਾਜਾ ਆਪ ਨਿਤਰਿਆ। (ਇੰਜ ਪ੍ਰਤੀਤ ਹੋਣ ਲਗਾ ਕਿ ਹੁਣ ਜੋ ਉਹ ਕਰੇਗਾ) ਉਹੀ ਹੋਏਗਾ ॥੩੮॥੧੯੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[39,195],"number_text":"੩੯। ੧੯੫।","page":231,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਵ ਦੂਤੀ ਇਤਿ ਦ੍ਰੁਗਾ ਬੁਲਾਈ। ਕਾਨ ਲਾਗਿ ਨੀਕੈ ਸਮੁਝਾਈ।","roman":"Siv dootee iti drugaa bulaaee | kaan laagi neekai samujhaaee |","meaning_en":"Here Durga called Shivduti, and explained to her well, whispering in her ear:","page":231,"flags":[{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Shivduti: a form of the goddess; literally 'she whose messenger is Shiva'.","meaning_pa":"ਦੇਵੀ ਦੁਰਗਾ ਨੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਕੋਲ ਸ਼ਿਵ-ਦੂਤੀ ਨੂੰ ਬੁਲਾਇਆ। (ਉਸ ਨੂੰ) ਕੰਨ ਵਿਚ (ਇਹ ਗੱਲ) ਚੰਗੀ ਤਰ੍ਹਾ ਸਮਝਾਈ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਵ ਕੋ ਭੇਜ ਦੀਜੀਐ ਤਹਾ। ਦੈਤ ਰਾਜ ਇਸਥਿਤ ਹੈ ਜਹਾ। ੩੯। ੧੯੫।","roman":"Siv ko bhej deejeeai tahaa | dait raaj isthit hai jahaa | 39 | 195 |","meaning_en":"'Send Shiva there, where the demon king is staying.' 39. 195.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿ ਸ਼ਿਵ ਨੂੰ ਉਥੇ ਭੇਜ ਦਿਓ ਜਿਥੇ ਦੈਂਤ-ਰਾਜਾ ਖੜੋਤਾ ਹੈ ॥੩੯॥੧੯੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[40,196],"number_text":"੪੦। ੧੯੬।","page":231,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਵ ਦੂਤੀ ਜਬ ਇਮ ਸੁਨ ਪਾਵਾ। ਸਿਵਹਿੰ ਦੂਤ ਕਰਿ ਉਤੈ ਪਠਾਵਾ।","roman":"Siv dootee jab im sun paavaa | sivhin doot kari utai pathaavaa |","meaning_en":"When Shivduti heard this, she made Shiva her messenger and sent him there;","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸ਼ਿਵ-ਦੂਤੀ ਨੇ ਜਦ ਇਹ ਸੁਣਿਆ (ਤਦ) ਸ਼ਿਵ ਨੂੰ ਦੂਤ ਬਣਾ ਕੇ ਉਥੇ ਭੇਜ ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਵ ਦੂਤੀ ਤਾਤੇ ਭਯੋ ਨਾਮਾ। ਜਾਨਤ ਸਕਲ ਪੁਰੁਖ ਅਰੁ ਬਾਮਾ। ੪੦। ੧੯੬।","roman":"Siv dootee taate bhayo naamaa | jaanat sakal purukh aru baamaa | 40 | 196 |","meaning_en":"from this came her name, Shivduti, known to all men and women. 40. 196.","page":231,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਦ ਤੋਂ (ਦੁਰਗਾ ਦਾ) ਨਾ ਸ਼ਿਵ-ਦੂਤੀ ਪੈ ਗਿਆ। ਇਸ ਗੱਲ ਨੂੰ ਸਭ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਅਤੇ ਮਰਦ ਜਾਣਦੇ ਹਨ ॥੪੦॥੧੯੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[41,197],"number_text":"੪੧। ੧੯੭।","page":232,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਵ ਕਹੀ ਦੈਤ ਰਾਜ ਸੁਨਿ ਬਾਤਾ। ਇਹ ਬਿਧਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਤੁਮਹੁ ਜਗਮਾਤਾ।","roman":"Siv kahee dait raaj suni baataa | ih bidhi kahiyo tumhu jagmaataa |","meaning_en":"Shiva said, 'Demon king, hear what I say; the Mother of the World has told you this:","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸ਼ਿਵ ਨੇ (ਜਾ ਕੇ) ਕਿਹਾ ਕਿ ਹੇ ਦੈਂਤ-ਰਾਜੇ, (ਮੇਰੀ) ਗੱਲ ਸੁਣ, ਤੈਨੂੰ ਦੁਰਗਾ ਮਾਤਾ ਨੇ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾ ਕਿਹਾ ਹੈ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਵਨ ਕੇ ਦੈ ਕੈ ਠਕੁਰਾਈ। ਕੈ ਮਾਂਡਹੁ ਹਮ ਸੰਗ ਲਰਾਈ। ੪੧। ੧੯੭।","roman":"Devan ke dai kai thakuraaee | kai maandhu ham sang laraaee | 41 | 197 |","meaning_en":"either give back their sovereignty to the gods, or wage battle with us.' 41. 197.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿ ਜਾ ਤਾ ਦੇਵਤਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਬਾਦਸ਼ਾਹੀ ਦੇ ਦਿਉ ਜਾ ਫਿਰ ਮੇਰੇ ਨਾਲ ਯੁੱਧ ਕਰੋ ॥੪੧॥੧੯੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[42,198],"number_text":"੪੨।੧੯੮।","page":232,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੈਤ ਰਾਜ ਇਹ ਬਾਤ ਨ ਮਾਨੀ। ਆਪ ਚਲੇ ਜੂਝਨ ਅਭਿਮਾਨੀ।","roman":"Dait raaj ih baat na maanee | aap chale joojhan abhimaanee |","meaning_en":"The demon king did not accept this; the proud one went himself to fight;","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੈਂਤ-ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ ਇਹ ਗੱਲ ਨਾ ਮੰਨੀ। (ਉਹ) ਅਭਿਮਾਨੀ (ਦੁਰਗਾ ਨਾਲ) ਲੜਨ ਲਈ ਆਪ ਤੁਰ ਪਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਰਜਤ ਕਾਲਿ ਕਾਲ ਜ੍ਯੋ ਜਹਾ। ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤਿ ਭਯੋ ਅਸੁਰ ਪਤਿ ਤਹਾ। ੪੨।੧੯੮।","roman":"Garjat kaali kaal jyo jahaa | praapti bhayo asur pati tahaa | 42 | 198 |","meaning_en":"where Kali was roaring like Death, there the demon lord arrived. 42. 198.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਥੇ ਕਾਲਕਾ ਕਾਲ ਵਾਗ ਗਰਜ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ, ਉਥੇ ਦੈਂਤ-ਰਾਜਾ ਜਾ ਪਹੁੰਚਿਆ ॥੪੨॥੧੯੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[43,199],"number_text":"੪੩। ੧੯੯।","page":232,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਮਕੀ ਤਹਾ ਅਸਨ ਕੀ ਧਾਰਾ। ਨਾਚੇ ਭੂਤ ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਬੈਤਾਰਾ।","roman":"Chamkee tahaa asan kee dhaaraa | naache bhoot pret baitaaraa |","meaning_en":"There the edges of swords flashed; ghosts, spirits and vetals danced;","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਥੇ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨਾ ਦੀ ਧਾਰ ਚਮਕ ਪਈ। ਭੂਤ, ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਅਤੇ ਬੈਤਾਲ ਨਚਣ ਲਗ ਪਏ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਫਰਕੇ ਅੰਧ ਕਬੰਧ ਅਚੇਤਾ। ਭਿਭਰੇ ਭਈਰਵ ਭੀਮ ਅਨੇਕਾ। ੪੩। ੧੯੯।","roman":"Pharke andh kabandh achetaa | bhibhre bhaeerav bheem anekaa | 43 | 199 |","meaning_en":"blind headless trunks quivered, senseless; many terrible Bhairavs roamed about. 43. 199.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਿਭਰੇ: read as 'roamed/rejoiced'; uncertain. Printed ਅਨੇਕਾ breaks the rhyme with ਅਚੇਤਾ; printed so.","meaning_pa":"ਅੰਨ੍ਹੇਵਾਹ ਧੜ ਅਚੇਤ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਤੜਫਣ ਲਗੇ। ਅਨੇਕਾ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਅਤੇ ਵੱਡੇ ਆਕਾਰ ਵਾਲੇ ਭੈਰੋ ਬੋਲਣ ਲਗ ਗਏ ॥੪੩॥੧੯੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[44,200],"number_text":"੪੪। ੨੦੦।","page":232,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਰਹੀ ਢੋਲ ਨਗਾਰੇ ਬਾਜੇ। ਭਾਤਿ ਭਾਤਿ ਜੋਧਾ ਰਣਿ ਗਾਜੈ।","roman":"Turhee dhol nagaare baaje | bhaati bhaati jodhaa rani gaajai |","meaning_en":"Trumpets, drums and war-drums sounded; warriors of every kind roared on the field;","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੁਰੀਆਂ, ਢੋਲ, ਨਗਾਰੇ ਵਜਣ ਲਗੇ, ਭਾਤ ਭਾਤ ਦੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿਚ ਗਜਣ ਲਗੇ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਢਡਿ ਡਫ ਡਮਰੁ ਡੁਗਡੁਗੀ ਘਨੀ। ਨਾਇ ਨਫੀਰੀ ਜਾਤ ਨ ਗਨੀ। ੪੪। ੨੦੦।","roman":"Dhadi daph damru dugdugee ghanee | naai napheeree jaat na ganee | 44 | 200 |","meaning_en":"many dhad, daf, damaru and dugdugi drums, and pipes and horns beyond counting. 44. 200.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Names of drums and pipes; ਨਾਇ: a pipe.","meaning_pa":"ਅਣਗਿਣਤ ਢੱਢਾ, ਡੱਫਾ, ਡਮਰੂ ਅਤੇ ਡੁਗਡੁਗੀਆਂ, ਸ਼ਹਿਨਾਈਆਂ, ਤੂਤੀਆਂ ਵਜਣ ਲਗ ਗਈਆਂ ॥੪੪॥੨੦੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਮਧੁਭਾਰ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਮਧੁਭਾਰ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Madhubhaar chhand","meaning_en":"Madhubhar metre.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਧੁਭਾਰ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[45,201],"number_text":"੪੫। ੨੦੧।","page":232,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹੁੰਕੇ ਕਿਕਾਣ। ਧੁੰਕੇ ਨਿਸਾਣ।","roman":"Hunke kikaan | dhunke nisaan |","meaning_en":"Horses neighed; war-drums boomed;","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਘੋੜੇ ਹਿਣਕ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ, ਧੌਂਸੇ ਗੂੰਜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਜੇ ਸੁ ਬੀਰ। ਗਜੇ ਗਹੀਰ। ੪੫। ੨੦੧।","roman":"Saje su beer | gaje gaheer | 45 | 201 |","meaning_en":"fine warriors were arrayed, roaring deeply. 45. 201.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਮੇ ਸੱਜੇ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ, ਗੰਭੀਰ (ਸੁਰ ਨਾਲ) ਗਜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ॥੪੫॥੨੦੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[46,202],"number_text":"੪੬। ੨੦੨।","page":232,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਝੁਕੇ ਨਿਝਕ। ਬਜੇ ਉਬਕ।","roman":"Jhuke nijhak | baje ubak |","meaning_en":"They pressed forward without hesitation; they struck without restraint;","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਉਬਕ: 'unrestrained' or a sound-word; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਨਿਝੱਕ ਹੋ ਕੇ (ਇਕ ਦੂਜੇ ਉਤੇ) ਝੁਕੇ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ, ਸਚੇਤ ਯੋਧੇ ('ਉਬਕ') ਭਿੜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਜੇ ਸੁਬਾਹ। ਅਛੈ ਉਛਾਹ। ੪੬। ੨੦੨।","roman":"Saje subaah | achhai uchhaah | 46 | 202 |","meaning_en":"the strong-armed were arrayed, with undying zeal. 46. 202.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੁੰਦਰ ਯੋਧੇ ਸੱਜੇ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ, ਅਪੱਛਰਾਵਾ ਦਾ ਉਤਸਾਹ ਵਧ ਰਿਹਾ ਸੀ ॥੪੬॥੨੦੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[47,203],"number_text":"੪੭। ੨੦੩।","page":232,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਟੇ ਕਿਕਾਣ। ਫੁਟੈ ਚਵਾਣ।","roman":"Kate kikaan | phutai chavaan |","meaning_en":"Horses were cut down; jaws were smashed;","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਵਾਣ: read as 'jaws' or 'whips'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਕਈ) ਘੋੜੇ ਕਟੇ ਪਏ ਸਨ, (ਕਈਆਂ ਦੇ) ਮੂੰਹ ਫਟੇ ਪਏ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੂਲੰ ਸੜਾਕ। ਉਠੇ ਕੜਾਕ। ੪੭। ੨੦੩।","roman":"Soolan saraak | uthe karaak | 47 | 203 |","meaning_en":"tridents hissed; crashing rose. 47. 203.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਕਿਤੇ) ਤ੍ਰਿਸ਼ੂਲ ਦੀ ਸੜਾਕ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਸੀ ਅਤੇ (ਕਿਤੇ) ਕੜਾਕ (ਦੀ ਆਵਾਜ਼) ਉਠਦੀ ਸੀ ॥੪੭॥੨੦੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[48,204],"number_text":"੪੮। ੨੦੪।","page":232,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਜੇ ਜੁਆਣ। ਬਜੇ ਨਿਸਾਣਿ।","roman":"Gaje juaan | baje nisaani |","meaning_en":"Young warriors roared; the war-drums sounded;","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੁਆਨ ਗੱਜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ, ਧੌਂਸੇ ਵਜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਜੇ ਰਜੇਂਦ੍ਰ। ਗਜੇ ਗਜੇਂਦ੍ਰ। ੪੮। ੨੦੪।","roman":"Saje rajendr | gaje gajendr | 48 | 204 |","meaning_en":"the great kings were arrayed; the great elephants trumpeted. 48. 204.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜੇ ਸਜੇ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ, ਹਾਥੀਆਂ ਵਾਲੇ ਸੈਨਾਪਤੀ ਗਜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ॥੪੮॥੨੦੪॥ ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB","note_pa":"ਇਹ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਪੰਕਤੀ ਸਮੇਤ ਉੱਪਰਲੀਆਂ 2 ਪੰਕਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਹੈ।"},{"type":"verse","number":[49,205],"number_text":"੪੯।੨੦੫।","page":232,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਫਿਰੇ ਬਾਜੀਯੰ ਤਾਜੀਯੰ ਇਤ ਉਤੰ। ਗਜੇ ਬਾਰਣੰ ਦਾਰੁਣੰ ਰਾਜ ਪੁਤ੍ਰੰ।","roman":"Phire baajeeyan taajeeyan it utan | gaje baarnan daarunan raaj putran |","meaning_en":"Horses, Arab steeds, wheeled here and there; elephants trumpeted, and fierce princes;","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਤਮ ਅਰਬੀ ਘੋੜੇ ਇਧਰ ਉਧਰ ਫਿਰਦੇ ਸਨ, ਰਾਜ-ਪੁੱਤਰਾ ਦੇ ਹਾਥੀ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਢੰਗ ਨਾਲ ਗਰਜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਜੇ ਸੰਖ ਭੇਰੀ ਉਠੈ ਸੰਖ ਨਾਦੰ। ਰਣੰਕੈ ਨਫੀਰੀ ਧੁਣ ਨਿਰਬਿਖਾਦੰ। ੪੯।੨੦੫।","roman":"Baje sankh bheree uthai sankh naadan | ranankai napheeree dhun nirbikhaadan | 49 | 205 |","meaning_en":"conches and trumpets sounded, the blare of conches rose; pipes rang out, their sound undaunted. 49. 205.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭੇਰੀਆਂ ਅਤੇ ਸੰਖ ਵਜ ਰਹੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਸੰਖਾ ਵਿਚ ਨਾਦ ਨਿਕਲ ਰਿਹਾ ਸੀ। ਤੂਤੀਆਂ ਦੀ ਧੁਨੀ ਨਿਰੰਤਰ ਚਲ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ ॥੪੯॥੨੦੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[50,206],"number_text":"੫੦। ੨੦੬।","page":232,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੜਕੇ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣੰ ਸੜਕਾਰ ਸੇਲੰ। ਉਠੀ ਕੂਹ ਜੂਹੰ ਭਈ ਰੇਲ ਪੇਲੰ।","roman":"Karke kripaanan sarkaar selan | uthee kooh joohan bhaee rel pelan |","meaning_en":"Swords crashed, spears hissed; cries rose from the hosts, and there was pushing and shoving;","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰੇਲ ਪੇਲੰ: 'jostling, pressing'.","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾ ਕੜ-ਕੜ ਕਰਦੀਆਂ ਸਨ, ਬਰਛੇ ਸੜ-ਸੜ ਕਰਦੇ ਸਨ। ਯੁੱਧ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿਚ ਰੌਲਾ ਪੈ ਗਿਆ ਸੀ, ਧਕਮ-ਧਕੀ ਹੋ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੁਲੇ ਤਛ ਮੁਛੰ ਗਿਰੇ ਚਉਰ ਚੀਰੰ। ਕਹੂੰ ਹਥ ਮਥੰ ਕਹੂੰ ਬਰਮ ਬੀਰੰ। ੫੦। ੨੦੬।","roman":"Rule tachh muchhan gire chaur cheeran | kahoon hath mathan kahoon baram beeran | 50 | 206 |","meaning_en":"the hacked and mangled rolled about, fly-whisks and garments fell; here hands and heads, there armour and warriors. 50. 206.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਕਿਤੇ) ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਦੇ ਟੋਟੇ ਰੁਲ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਕਿਤੇ ਚੌਰ ਅਤੇ ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਡਿਗੇ ਪਏ ਸਨ। ਕਿਤੇ ਹੱਥ ਅਤੇ ਸਿਰ ਅਤੇ ਕਿਤੇ ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਦੇ ਕਵਚ ('ਬਰਮ') (ਡਿਗੇ ਪਏ ਸਨ।) ॥੫੦॥੨੦੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"Rasaval metre.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[51,207],"number_text":"੫੧। ੨੦੭।","page":232,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਲੀ ਬੈਰ ਰੁਝੇ। ਸਮੂਹ ਸਾਰ ਜੁਝੇ।","roman":"Balee bair rujhe | samooh saar jujhe |","meaning_en":"The mighty ones were locked in enmity; all fought with steel;","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਮੂਹ: 'all together' or 'face to face'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਬਲਵਾਨ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਵੈਰ ਭਾਵ ਨਾਲ ਉਲਝ ਪਏ ਸਨ, ਸਾਰੇ ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰਾ ਨਾਲ ਜੂਝ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਭਾਰੇ ਹਥੀਯਾਰੰ। ਬਕੈ ਮਾਰੁ ਮਾਰੰ। ੫੧। ੨੦੭।","roman":"Sanbhaare hatheeyaaran | bakai maaru maaran | 51 | 207 |","meaning_en":"they took up weapons, crying 'Kill! Kill!' 51. 207.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਥਿਆਰਾ ਨੂੰ ਸੰਭਾਲ ਕੇ ਮਾਰੋ-ਮਾਰੋ ਦਾ ਰੌਲਾ ਪਾ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ॥੫੧॥੨੦੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[52,208],"number_text":"੫੨। ੨੦੮।","page":232,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬੈ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਜੇ। ਮਹਾਬੀਰ ਗਜੇ।","roman":"Sabai sasatr saje | mahaabeer gaje |","meaning_en":"All were armed with weapons; great warriors roared;","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਮਹਾਨ ਯੋਧੇ ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਜਾ ਕੇ ਗਰਜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰੰ ਓਘ ਛੁਟੇ। ਕੜਕਾਰੁ ਉਠੇ। ੫੨। ੨੦੮।","roman":"Saran ogh chhute | karkaaru uthe | 52 | 208 |","meaning_en":"floods of arrows were loosed; crashing rose. 52. 208.","page":232,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੀਰਾ ਦੀ ਵਾਛੜ ਹੋ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ, ਕਾੜ-ਕਾੜ (ਦੀ ਧੁਨੀ) ਉਠ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ ॥੫੨॥੨੦੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[53,209],"number_text":"੫੩। ੨੦੯।","page":233,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਜੈ ਬਾਦ੍ਰਿਤੇਅੰ। ਹਸੈ ਗਾਧ੍ਰਬੇਅੰ।","roman":"Bajai baadritean | hasai gaadhrabean |","meaning_en":"Musical instruments sound; the gandharvas laugh;","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਦ੍ਰਿਤੇਅੰ: read as 'instruments' (vaditra); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਵਾਜੇ ਵਜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ, ਗੰਧਰਬ ਹਸ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਝੰਡਾ ਗਡ ਜੁਟੇ। ਸਰੰ ਸੰਜ ਫੁਟੇ। ੫੩। ੨੦੯।","roman":"Jhandaa gad jute | saran sanj phute | 53 | 209 |","meaning_en":"planting their banners, they engage; arrows pierce through armour. 53. 209.","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੰਜ: 'armour'.","meaning_pa":"(ਸੂਰਮੇ) ਝੰਡੇ ਗਡ ਕੇ (ਆਪਸ ਵਿਚ) ਜੁਟੇ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ, ਤੀਰਾ ਨਾਲ ਕਵਚ ਫੁਟ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ॥੫੩॥੨੦੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[54,210],"number_text":"੫੪। ੨੧੦।","page":233,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਹੂੰ ਓਰ ਉਠੇ। ਸਰੰ ਬ੍ਰਿਸਟ ਬੁਠੇ।","roman":"Chahoon or uthe | saran brisat buthe |","meaning_en":"They rose on all four sides and rained showers of arrows;","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਸੂਰਵੀਰ) ਚੌਹਾ ਪਾਸਿਆਂ ਤੋਂ ਖੜੋ ਗਏ ਸਨ, ਤੀਰਾ ਦੀ ਬਰਖਾ ਕਰ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੋਧੀ ਕਰਾਲੰ। ਬਕੈ ਬਿਕਰਾਲੰ। ੫੪। ੨੧੦।","roman":"Karodhee karaalan | bakai bikraalan | 54 | 210 |","meaning_en":"the wrathful, fearsome ones shouted terrible words. 54. 210.","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰੋਧੀ ਅਤੇ ਭਿਆਨਕ (ਵੀਰ ਯੋਧੇ) ਬਕਵਾਦ ਕਰ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ॥੫੪॥੨੧੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[55,211],"number_text":"੫੫। ੨੧੧।","page":233,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਕੁਠੀਅੰ ਬੁਠੀਅੰ ਬ੍ਰਿਸਟ ਬਾਣੰ। ਰਣੰ ਡੁਲੀਯੰ ਬਾਜ ਖਾਲੀ ਪਲਾਣੰ।","roman":"Kite kutheean butheean brisat baanan | ranan duleeyan baaj khaalee palaanan |","meaning_en":"Many were struck down as arrows rained down; on the field horses wandered with empty saddles;","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ (ਵੀਰ) ਕੁਠੇ ਜਾ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ, (ਕਿਤੇ) ਬਾਣਾ ਦਾ ਮੀਂਹ ਵਰ੍ਹ ਰਿਹਾ ਸੀ। (ਕਿਤੇ) ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿਚ ਖਾਲੀ ਕਾਠੀਆਂ ਵਾਲੇ ਘੋੜੇ ਫਿਰਦੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਝੇ ਜੋਧਿਯੰ ਬੀਰ ਦੇਵੰ ਅਦੇਵੰ। ਸਭੇ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਾਜਾ ਮਨੋ ਸਾਂਤਨੇਵੰ। ੫੫। ੨੧੧।","roman":"Jujhe jodhiyan beer devan adevan | sabhe sasatr saajaa mano saantnevan | 55 | 211 |","meaning_en":"warriors fought, heroes both of the gods and of the demons, all armed as if each were Bhishma, son of Shantanu. 55. 211.","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਾਂਤਨੇਵੰ: Bhishma, son of Shantanu.","meaning_pa":"ਦੈਂਤ ਅਤੇ ਦੇਵਤੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ (ਆਪਸ ਵਿਚ) ਲੜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ। ਸਭ ਨੇ ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਜਾਏ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ। (ਇੰਜ ਪ੍ਰਤੀਤ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਸੀ) ਮਾਨੋ ਭੀਸ਼ਣ ਪਿਤਾਮਾ ('ਸਾਤਨੇਵੰ') ਹੋਣ ॥੫੫॥੨੧੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[56,212],"number_text":"੫੬। ੨੧੨।","page":233,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਜੇ ਗਜੀਯੰ ਸਰਬ ਸਜੇ ਪਵੰਗੰ। ਜੁਧੰ ਜੁਟੀਯੰ ਜੋਧ ਛੁਟੇ ਖਤੰਗੰ।","roman":"Gaje gajeeyan sarab saje pavangan | judhan juteeyan jodh chhute khatangan |","meaning_en":"Elephants trumpeted; all the horses were arrayed; warriors joined battle and arrows flew;","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਗਾਜੀ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਸਨ, (ਉਨ੍ਹਾ ਦੇ) ਘੋੜੇ ਸਜੇ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ, ਯੋਧੇ ਯੁੱਧ ਵਿਚ ਜੁਟੇ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਤੀਰ ਛੁਟ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੜਕੇ ਤਬਲੰ ਝੜੰਕੇ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣੰ। ਸੜਕਾਰ ਸੇਲੰ ਰਣੰਕੇ ਨਿਸਾਣੰ। ੫੬। ੨੧੨।","roman":"Tarke tablan jharanke kripaanan | sarkaar selan rananke nisaanan | 56 | 212 |","meaning_en":"drums cracked and swords clanged; spears hissed and war-drums rang. 56. 212.","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਬਲੇ ਵਜਦੇ ਸਨ, ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨਾ ਝਟਕ ਰਹੀਆਂ ਸਨ, ਬਰਛੇ ਸਰੜ ਸਰੜ ਕਰਦੇ ਸਨ, ਧੌਂਸੇ ਗੂੰਜਦੇ ਸਨ ॥੫੬॥੨੧੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[57,213],"number_text":"੫੭।੨੧੩।","page":233,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਢਮਾ ਢਮ ਢੋਲੰ ਢਲਾ ਢੁਕ ਢਾਲੰ। ਗਹਾ ਜੂਹ ਗਜੇ ਹਯੰ ਹਲਚਾਲੰ।","roman":"Dhamaa dham dholan dhalaa dhuk dhaalan | gahaa jooh gaje hayan halchaalan |","meaning_en":"Drums boomed, shields clashed; the hosts surged, elephants trumpeted, horses were in commotion;","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਹਾ ਜੂਹ: 'the throng pressed'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਢਮ-ਢਮ ਢੋਲ ਅਤੇ ਢਕ-ਢਕ ਢਾਲਾ (ਵਜ ਰਹੀਆਂ ਸਨ)। ਹਾਥੀਆਂ ('ਗਹਾ') ਦੇ ਸਮੂਹ ਗਰਜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਘੋੜਿਆਂ ਵਿਚ ਹਲ-ਚਲ ਮਚੀ ਹੋਈ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਟਾ ਸਟ ਸੈਲੰ ਖਹਾ ਖੂਨਿ ਖਗੰ। ਤੁਟੇ ਚਰਮ ਬਰਮੰ ਉਠੇ ਨਾਲ ਅਗੰ। ੫੭।੨੧੩।","roman":"Sataa sat sailan khahaa khooni khagan | tute charam barman uthe naal agan | 57 | 213 |","meaning_en":"spears struck again and again, bloody swords clashed; shields and armour broke, and fire rose from the gun-barrels. 57. 213.","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਾਲ ਅਗੰ: 'fire from the barrels (of guns)'.","meaning_pa":"ਬਰਛਿਆਂ ਦੀ ਸਟ ਤੇ ਸਟ ਪੈ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ, ਖੂਨ ਰੰਗੀਆਂ ਤਲਵਾਰਾ (ਆਪਸ ਵਿਚ) ਖਹਿੰਦੀਆਂ ਸਨ। ਢਾਲਾ ਅਤੇ ਕਵਚ ਟੁਟੇ ਪਏ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਬੰਦੂਕਾ ਵਿਚੋਂ ਅੱਗ ਨਿਕਲ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ ॥੫੭॥੨੧੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[58,214],"number_text":"੫੮। ੨੧੪।","page":233,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠੇ ਅਗਿ ਨਾਲੰ ਖਹੇ ਖੋਲ ਖਗੰ। ਨਿਸਾ ਮਾਵਸੀ ਜਾਣੁ ਮਾਸਾਣ ਜਗੰ।","roman":"Uthe agi naalan khahe khol khagan | nisaa maavsee jaanu maasaan jagan |","meaning_en":"Fire rose from the barrels; swords clashed on helmets; it was like the cremation ground lit up on the night of the new moon;","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖੋਲ: 'helmet'; ਮਾਵਸੀ: amavas, the moonless night.","meaning_pa":"(ਸਿਰ ਦੇ) ਟੋਪਾ (ਖੋਲ) ਉਤੇ ਤਲਵਾਰਾ ਵਜਦੀਆਂ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਅੱਗ ਦੀਆਂ ਚਿੰਗਾਰੀਆਂ ਨਿਕਲਦੀਆਂ ਸਨ, ਮਾਨੋ ਮਸਿਆ ਦੀ ਰਾਤ ('ਨਿਸਾ') ਸਮਝ ਕੇ ਭੂਤ-ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਜਾਗ ਪਏ ਹੋਣ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਕੀ ਡਾਕਣੀ ਡਾਮਰੂ ਡਉਰ ਡਕੰ। ਨਚੇ ਬੀਰ ਬੈਤਾਲ ਭੂਤੰ ਭਭਕੰ। ੫੮। ੨੧੪।","roman":"Dakee daaknee daamroo daur dakan | nache beer baitaal bhootan bhabhkan | 58 | 214 |","meaning_en":"the dakinis howled, the damaru drums rattled; the vetals and ghosts danced and shrieked. 58. 214.","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਡਾਕਣੀਆਂ ਡਕਾਰਨ ਲਗੀਆਂ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਡਮਰੂ ਡਕ-ਡਕ ਕਰਦੇ ਵਜ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ। ਬੀਰ, ਬੈਤਾਲ ਅਤੇ ਭੂਤ ਭਭਕਾ ਮਾਰਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਨਚ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ ॥੫੮॥੨੧੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਬੇਲੀ ਬਿਦ੍ਰਮ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਬੇਲੀ ਬਿਦ੍ਰਮ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Belee bidram chhand","meaning_en":"Beli Bidram metre.","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬੇਲੀ ਬਿਦ੍ਰਮ ਛੰਦ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[59,215],"number_text":"੫੯। ੨੧੫।","page":233,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰਬ ਸਸਤ੍ਰੁ ਆਵਤ ਭੇ ਜਿਤੇ। ਸਭ ਕਾਟਿ ਦੀਨ ਦ੍ਰੁਗਾ ਤਿਤੇ।","roman":"Sarab sastru aavat bhe jite | sabh kaati deen drugaa tite |","meaning_en":"All the weapons that came at her, Durga cut them all down;","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਤਨੇ ਵੀ ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰਾ (ਦੇ ਵਾਰ) ਹੋ ਰਹੇ ਸਨ, ਉਤਨੇ ਹੀ ਦੁਰਗਾ ਨੇ ਸਭ ਕਟ ਦਿੱਤੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਿ ਅਉਰ ਜੇਤਿਕੁ ਡਾਰੀਅੰ। ਤੇਉ ਕਾਟਿ ਭੂਮਿ ਉਤਾਰੀਅੰ। ੫੯। ੨੧੫।","roman":"Ari aur jetiku daareean | teu kaati bhoomi utaareean | 59 | 215 |","meaning_en":"and all the other weapons the foe threw, she cut and brought down to the ground. 59. 215.","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੋਰ ਵੀ ਜਿਤਨੇ (ਅਸਤ੍ਰ) ਵੈਰੀ ਸੁਟਦੇ ਸਨ, ਉਨ੍ਹਾ ਨੂੰ ਕਟ ਕੇ ਭੂਮੀ ਉਤੇ ਸੁਟ ਦਿੰਦੀ ਸੀ ॥੫੯॥੨੧੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[60,216],"number_text":"੬੦।੨੧੬।","page":233,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰ ਆਪ ਕਾਲੀ ਛੰਡੀਅੰ। ਸਰਬਾਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਤ੍ਰ ਬਿਹੰਡੀਅੰ।","roman":"Sar aap kaalee chhandeean | sarbaasatr satr bihandeean |","meaning_en":"Kali herself loosed arrows and destroyed all the enemy's weapons;","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਲੀ ਨੇ ਆਪ ਬਾਣ ਛਡੇ ਸਨ, ਵੈਰੀ ਦੇ ਸਾਰੇ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਤੋੜ ਫੋੜ ਦਿੱਤੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਹੀਨ ਜਬੈ ਨਿਹਾਰਿਯੋ। ਜੈ ਸਬਦ ਦੇਵਨ ਉਚਾਰਿਯੋ। ੬੦।੨੧੬।","roman":"Sasatr heen jabai nihaariyo | jai sabad devan uchaariyo | 60 | 216 |","meaning_en":"when they saw him weaponless, the gods raised the cry of victory. 60. 216.","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦੋਂ (ਦੇਵਤਿਆਂ ਨੇ ਸੁੰਭ ਨੂੰ) ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰਾ ਤੋਂ ਬਿਨਾ ਵੇਖਿਆ, (ਤਦੋਂ) ਦੇਵਤਿਆਂ ਨੇ (ਦੁਰਗਾ ਦਾ) ਜੈ-ਘੋਸ਼ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤਾ ॥੬੦॥੨੧੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[61,217],"number_text":"੬੧। ੨੧੭।","page":233,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਭਿ ਮਧਿ ਬਾਜਨ ਬਾਜਹੀ। ਅਵਿਲੋਕਿ ਦੇਵਾ ਗਾਜਹੀ।","roman":"Nabhi madhi baajan baajhee | aviloki devaa gaajhee |","meaning_en":"In the sky instruments sounded; seeing it, the gods shouted for joy;","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਆਕਾਸ਼ ਵਿਚ ਵਾਜੇ ਵਜਦੇ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ (ਇਹ ਦ੍ਰਿਸ਼) ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਦੇਵਤੇ ਗਜਣ ਲਗ ਗਏ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਖਿ ਦੇਵ ਬਾਰੰ ਬਾਰਹੀ। ਜੈ ਸਬਦ ਸਰਬ ਪੁਕਾਰਹੀ। ੬੧। ੨੧੭।","roman":"Lakhi dev baaran baarhee | jai sabad sarab pukaarhee | 61 | 217 |","meaning_en":"watching, the gods all cried 'Victory!' again and again. 61. 217.","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਦੇਵਤੇ (ਦੇਵੀ ਨੂੰ) ਬਾਰ ਬਾਰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਜੈ ਦਾ ਘੋਸ਼ ਕਰਨ ਲਗ ਗਏ ਸਨ ॥੬੧॥੨੧੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[62,218],"number_text":"੬੨। ੨੧੮।","page":233,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਿ ਕੋਪਿ ਕਾਲ ਕਰਾਲੀਯੰ। ਖਟ ਅੰਗ ਪਾਣਿ ਉਛਾਲੀਯੰ।","roman":"Rani kopi kaal karaaleeyan | khat ang paani uchhaaleeyan |","meaning_en":"On the field the fearsome Kali, enraged, raised her sword in her hand,","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖਟ ਅੰਗ: read as khatang/khadag, a weapon (sword or club); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿਚ ਕਾਲੀ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਨਾਲ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਰੂਪ ਧਾਰ ਕੇ ਫਿਰ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ। (ਉਸ ਨੇ) ਛੇ ਹੱਥਾ ਅਤੇ ਭੁਜਾਵਾ ਨੂੰ ਉਤੇ ਉਛਾਲਿਆ ਹੋਇਆ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਰਿ ਸੁੰਭ ਹਥ ਦੁਛੰਡੀਯੰ। ਇਕ ਚੋਟਿ ਦੁਸਟ ਬਿਹੰਡੀਯੰ। ੬੨। ੨੧੮।","roman":"Siri sunbh hath duchhandeeyan | ik choti dusat bihandeeyan | 62 | 218 |","meaning_en":"and struck it on Sumbh's head; with one blow she destroyed the wicked one. 62. 218.","page":233,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਥ ਦੁਛੰਡੀਯੰ: 'struck with both hands' or 'struck with the hand'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਫਿਰ ਸੁੰਭ ਕੇ ਸਿਰ ਵਿਚ ਦੋਵੇਾਂ ਹੱਥ ਦੇ ਮਾਰੇ, ਇਕੋ ਸਟ ਨਾਲ ਦੁਸ਼ਟ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰ ਮੁਕਾਇਆ ॥੬੨॥੨੧੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":234,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[63,219],"number_text":"੬੩। ੨੧੯।","page":234,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਮ ਸੁੰਭਾਸੁਰ ਕੋ ਹਨਾ ਅਧਿਕ ਕੋਪ ਕੈ ਕਾਲਿ।","roman":"Jim sunbhaasur ko hanaa adhik kop kai kaali |","meaning_en":"Just as Kali, in great anger, slew Sumbhasur,","page":234,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਕਾਲੀ। ਜਿਵੇਾਂ (ਤੂੰ) ਬਹੁਤ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਸੁੰਭ ਦੈਂਤ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰਿਆ ਸੀ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਯੋ ਸਾਧਨ ਕੇ ਸਤ੍ਰੁ ਸਭ ਚਾਬਤ ਜਾਹ ਕਰਾਲ। ੬੩। ੨੧੯।","roman":"Tyo saadhan ke satru sabh chaabat jaah karaal | 63 | 219 |","meaning_en":"so may the fearsome one go on devouring all the enemies of the holy. 63. 219.","page":234,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਾਬਤ ਜਾਹ: 'go on chewing up'; read as a wish or statement."}]}],"ending":{"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਨਾਟਕੇ ਚੰਡੀ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰੇ ਸੁੰਭ ਬਧਹ","roman":"Iti sree bachitr naatke chandee charitre sunbh badhah","meaning_en":"Here ends, in Sri Bachittar Natak, in Chandi Charitr, the slaying of Sumbh,","page":234,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖਸਟਮੋ ਧਿਆਯ ਸੰਪੂਰਨਮ ਸਤੁ ਸੁਭਮ ਸਤੁ। ੬।","roman":"Khasatmo dhiaay sanpoornam satu subham satu | 6 |","meaning_en":"the sixth chapter, complete. All is well. 6.","page":234,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਤਿਵੇਾਂ) ਸੰਤਾ ਦੇ ਸਾਰੇ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਰੂਪ ਧਾਰ ਕੇ ਚਬ ਜਾਇਆ ਕਰ ॥੬੩॥੨੧੯॥ ਇਥੇ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਨਾਟਕ ਦੇ 'ਚੰਡੀ-ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰ' ਪ੍ਰਸੰਗ ਦੇ 'ਸੁੰਭ-ਬਧ' ਨਾ ਦੇ ਛੇਵੇਾਂ ਅਧਿਆਇ ਦੀ ਸ਼ੁਭ ਸਮਾਪਤੀ ॥੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB","note_pa":"ਇਹ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਪੰਕਤੀ ਸਮੇਤ ਉੱਪਰਲੀਆਂ 3 ਪੰਕਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਹੈ।"}],"page":234,"number":[6]}});
